    "ASHG GTEx Workshop Materials": "ASHG GTEx 研讨会的材料",
    "The Adult Genotype Tissue Expression (GTEx) Project is a comprehensive public resource to study human gene expression and regulation, and its relationship to genetic variation across multiple diverse tissues and individuals. GTEx donor recruitment and molecular data generation are complete for core molecular assays including WGS, WES, and RNA-seq.": "成人基因型-组织表达（GTEx）项目是一个综合性的公共资源，用于研究人类基因表达与调控及其与多种不同组织和个体间遗传变异的关系。GTEx 的供者招募以及核心分子检测（包括 WGS、WES 和 RNA-seq）的分子数据生成均已完成。",
    "The project collected samples from up to 54 non-diseased tissue sites across nearly 1,000 deceased individuals. All individuals were densely genotyped to assess genetic variation within their genomes by Whole Genome Sequencing (WGS). Gene expression of each tissue was assessed by RNA sequencing (bulk RNA-seq). Expression quantitative trait loci (eQTLs) were identified as genetic variants that were significantly correlated with changes in the expression of nearby genes. The project provides a comprehensive identification of tissue-shared and tissue-specific human eQTLs, as well as a valuable basis for the mechanistic interpretation of the many non-coding genetic variants that have been associated with common human diseases, such as heart disease, cancer, diabetes, asthma, and stroke.": "该项目从近 1,000 名已故个体中最多 54 个无疾病组织部位采集了样本。所有个体均通过全基因组测序（WGS）进行了高密度基因分型，以评估其基因组内的遗传变异。每个组织的基因表达通过 RNA 测序（bulk RNA-seq）进行评估。表达数量性状位点（eQTL）被鉴定为与邻近基因表达变化显著相关的遗传变异。该项目全面鉴定了组织共享型和组织特异性的人类 eQTL，并为解释许多与人类常见疾病（如心脏病、癌症、糖尿病、哮喘和中风）相关的非编码遗传变异提供了有价值的机制基础。",
    "Details about sample collections, exclusion/inclusion criteria, and pathology are described in: Carithers et al. (2015) .": "有关样本采集、排除/纳入标准和病理学的详细信息，见：Carithers 等（2015）。",
    "Additional data generation efforts that were funded to enhance the core GTEx data are described in: eGTEx Project (2017) .": "为增强核心 GTEx 数据而资助的其他数据生成工作，见：eGTEx 项目（2017）。",
    "Data generation, QC, and analysis methods are described in the Supplementary Material for The GTEx Consortium (2020) and also here.": "数据生成、质量控制（QC）和分析方法见 The GTEx Consortium（2020）的补充材料，另见此处。",
    "Much of the GTEx data and metadata are protected access (e.g., sequence data and complete donor metadata, etc.). Access to these data requires users to complete a data access request in dbGaP and then access the data in AnVIL .": "GTEx 的许多数据和元数据属于受保护访问（例如序列数据和完整的供者元数据等）。访问这些数据需要用户在 dbGaP 中完成数据访问申请，然后在 AnVIL 中访问数据。",
    "Open access GTEx data including expression counts and eQTLs are available for visual exploration and download on the GTEx Portal.": "包括表达计数和 eQTL 在内的开放访问 GTEx 数据，可在 GTEx Portal 上进行可视化探索和下载。",
    "Protocols used for tissue sampling are available here: GTEx Tissue Harvesting Work Instruction . Histology images and pathology QC notes are available here.": "组织采样所用的方案可在此处获取：GTEx Tissue Harvesting Work Instruction。组织学图像和病理 QC 记录可在此处获取。",
    "A subset of tissues from 16 donors were also characterized using single-cell RNA sequencing, as described in: Eraslen, et al. (2022) .": "来自 16 名供者的部分组织还通过单细胞 RNA 测序进行了表征，详见：Eraslen 等（2022）。",
    "All remaining collected tissue samples and derived nucleic acids are in a biobank and are available to be requested for future studies.": "所有其余已采集的组织样本和提取的核酸均保存在生物样本库中，可供申请用于未来的研究。",
    "The Genotype-Tissue Expression (GTEx) Project was supported by the Common Fund of the Office of the Director of the National Institutes of Health , and by the National Cancer Institute , the National Human Genome Research Institute , the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute , the National Institute on Drug Abuse , the National Institute of Mental Health , the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke .": "基因型-组织表达（GTEx）项目由美国国立卫生研究院院长办公室共同基金资助，并得到美国国家癌症研究所、美国国家人类基因组研究所、美国国家心肺血液研究所、美国国家药物滥用研究所、美国国家精神卫生研究所和美国国家神经疾病与中风研究所的支持。",
